gametitle=Madden NFL 2004 (SLUS-20752) [14F8B841]
comment=P9 -- per-frame drive on the doubled defender. Over P1+P4. Supersedes P8.
// P8's cave was sound but its host ran 1 frame in 7 (gates passed on 35
// frames, canary counted 5 -- measured, docs/motion-block-cave.md). P9 moves
// the SAME idea into the per-frame sweep at 0x001F2070, where P5/P6 proved
// s1 and s2 are the two members of an engagement EVERY frame.
// Gate: dt_role == 2 identifies the doubled defender; nothing else is
// touched, so single blocks and unpaired players are byte-identical.
// Step is a fixed 0.045 yd/frame -- deliberately a DIAGNOSTIC magnitude, not
// the weight+STR law. Prove the hook drives a body first; the law (D = clamp(
// margin + R^2 - 1, 0, 3), TE+RT vs DE = 2.42) layers on once it does.
// Canary 0x00514974 counts driven frames; expect ~56/play (the role pair's
// measured lifetime) against P8's 5.
// Cave #7 re-censused clean this session on five axes; P8's body is
// overwritten in place.

